<title>JAPAN: TABLE - Japan June M2+CD money supply up 2.8 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Japan June M2+CD money supply up 2.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's broadly defined money supply average of M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs) grew a preliminary 2.8 percent in June from a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of June money supply figures follows:</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     JUNE PRELIM   MAY REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2 + CDs     +2.8	   +3.1</p>
<p>   M1			 +8.6	   +9.0</p>
<p>   CDs		     +23.8	  +30.6</p>
<p>Broadest liquidity	+3.3	   +3.7</p>
<p>(Annualised month-on-month percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     JUNEPRELIM   MAY REVISED</p>
<p>Adjusted M2 + CDs	 +2.8	   +3.4</p>
<p>(Average outstanding yen levels)</p>
<p>			     JUNE PRELIM   MAY REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2+CDs	570.8 trln   569.2 trln</p>
<p>   M1			177.2 trln   178.8 trln</p>
<p>   CDs			18.4 trln    20.9 trln</p>
<p>			     JUNEPRELIM   MAY REVISED</p>
<p>Broadest liquidity     1,153.8 trln 1,152.4 trln</p>
<p>(NOTE: Broadest liquidity measure includes postal savings deposits at agricultural financial institutions and trust banks, bank debentures, Japanese government bonds, investment trusts and foreign bonds, along with M2 plus CDs.)</p>
</text>
